correction('P001221','654, number of cusps','Only1cusp for every real quadratic Hilbert modular quotient','One cusp requires class number1 for the full group; torsion-free covers may have more cusps','Cusps are ideal classes. Full group may have orbifold points; do not silently invoke a smooth-manifold index.')
correction('P001221','654, L-series domain',r'Unexplained final \(N_F\) in the summation domain',r'Use \((M\setminus\{0\})/V\) for the standard unit-orbit series','Mathematical emendation: without quotient, norm-one units give infinitely repeated terms. Exact L-value coefficient remains unverified.','ambiguity')
correction('P001221','655, Dolbeault exact sequence',r'Final \(H^1(T)\)',r'Final \(H^1(T^j)\)','The exponentj is missing in the scan, while every preceding term is for T^j.')
correction('P001222','655, Quillen metric',r"Squared cohomology norm divided by \(\det{}'\Delta_j\)",'Retain division: this is the dual of Quillen\'s original operator determinant-line convention','Quillen (1985), sections 1--3 checked in full. This row prevents an erroneous correction from division to multiplication.','ambiguity')
correction('P001223','656, lattice heading','Definition of a lattice includes the modular law','The final displayed implication is the additional modular axiom','Separates general lattice axioms from modularity.')
correction('P001224','656, first cubicle list','List begins with0','The empty meet is the cubicle top1; its relative bottom is the meet of allh_t','Gelfand--Ponomarev1974section1.3. Mapping every generator to V shows the relative cubicle bottom need not map to0.')
correction('P001224','656, recursion','Second-level exclusion usesi2; Gamma indices are scrambled','Use i1 in the second-level term and exclude i_j,i_{j+1} in Gamma; also require adjacent beta indices distinct','Exact source reconstruction from Gelfand--Ponomarev1974section1.3eqs.(1.1)--(1.3).')
correction('P001224','656, cubicle size',r'\(2^n\)',r'\(2^r\), r=number of generators','The theorem has2^r; n is unexplained in these notes.')
correction('P001225','657, central convention','Bracket(j-i) with positive(i^3-i)C, followed by standard-c formulas','If e_i=L_{-i}, then C=-c; convert later eigenvalues or change the initial bracket convention','Direct substitution into the usual Virasoro bracket. The algebra itself is valid; the linked formulas need one convention.','ambiguity')
correction('P001225','657, category name',r'\ru{Оре}','Retain uncertain reading; likely categoryO is not certain enough for a silent correction','The Russian transcription flags the same ambiguous word. No specific BGG paper is inferred.','ambiguity')
correction('P001225','657, Kac polynomial',r'\(\frac12(r^2-s^2)^2\)',r'\(\frac1{16}(r^2-s^2)^2\)','Scan confirms1/2; Feigin--Fuchs1982section3.2printedp.58has1/16. At c=1,r=1,s=2 the correct polynomial is(h-1/4)^2.')
correction('P001226','657, root quadratic sum',r'Inner \(r\in\Delta\)',r'Inner \(r\in\mathbb Z\)','Outer sum is over roots; inner variable labels loop modes. The scan itself has Delta.')
correction('P001226','657, enveloping algebra','Infinite S(m) is an element of the ordinary enveloping algebra','Use a completed enveloping algebra or its well-defined action on a restricted module','Normal-ordered infinite sums are not finite PBW sums; Kent1985p.133 supplies the construction.')
correction('P001227','657, Sugawara denominator',r'\(e_m=S(m)/(2(g+k))\) without restriction',r'Assume \(k\ne-h^\vee\), with invariant form and level normalized consistently','At the critical level the denominator vanishes; the raw Killing form is not the normalization with long-root length2.')
correction('P001227','657, sl2 highest weight',r'\(k=k_1+k_2\), \(h=k_1(k_1+1)/(k+2)\)',r'Affine Dynkin labelell gives h=ell(ell+2)/(4(k+2)); spinj=ell/2 gives j(j+1)/(k+2)','The same k1 cannot be both a Dynkin label in level sum and a spin without a factor2 conversion.')
correction('P001227','657, commuting subalgebra',r'\(\widehat{\mathfrak g}_i\)',r'\(\widehat{\mathfrak g}_1\)','Only subalgebra1 is defined; i is the running Virasoro mode.')
correction('P001227','657, Selberg integral',r'Vandermonde powerrho, limits0and1, printed Gamma product',r'Use power2rho on0<t1<...<tm<1; or cube with absolute values and m! times the printed product','Forrester--Warnaar2008eqs.(1.1)--(1.2). This is a paired exponent/domain correction; neither alone fixes the formula.')
correction('P001228','657, mixed-product range','Upperv=m+1','Upperv=n+m','Two species have sizesn andm; the erroneous endpoint is visible in scan.')
correction('P001228','657, last differential','dt1...dtn','dt1...dt_{n+m}','The integrand has n+m screening variables.')
correction('P001228','657, correlation order','Two-point correlation function','Four-point conformal block before the nonchiral combination','The same page then calls it four-point and defines the cross-ratio; two points have no such modulus.')
correction('P001228','657, screening integral','Unqualified ordinary real0--1integral with mixed double poles','Specify disjoint/compatible complex contours or twisted cycles and charge-neutrality/external-charge data','Dotsenko--Fateev1984section3. For both species present, crossing t_u=t_v gives a nonintegrable real double pole.')
correction('P001228','657, continuation claim','Analytic continuation from nonnegative integern,m gives the real functions','State a uniqueness class or independent definition; the discrete data alone do not select a continuation','Adding sin(pi*n)H(n,m) preserves every nonnegative integer pair. This records underdetermination, not a new open problem.','ambiguity')
